this little girl is Kwon ji-yong she's  woken up in a hospital bed after living  through the most terrifying ordeal of  her very young life  [Applause]  this is her 24 hours ago the  six-year-old was rescued from a sinking  ferry there were hundreds of passengers  on board including Kwan's mother and  father they haven't been heard from  since like so many others who were still  missing above the water this is all that  can be seen of the seawall she was on a  routine overnight crossing ferrying her  passengers between the mainland and Jeju  Island but just hours from shore with  land in sight disaster struck  [Music]  the ferry sank with more than 450 people  on board now some of her dead have been  returned to shore on board  many schoolchildren classmates on a  field trip together the search for them  and other passengers has continued  through the night and into a second day  with so many still missing there's hope  desperation that survivors will somehow  be found some families have even hired  their own boat to take them out to the  site of the disaster but with each  passing hour without news that hope  turns to fuel this man is the ferries  captain he doesn't want his face to be  seen but he did have these words for the  grief-stricken relatives I am really  sorry I'm deeply ashamed I don't know  what to say the apology will do nothing  to ease the distress of the families  they are without their loved ones and  they are without an explanation this  film taken by a passenger shows  terrified schoolchildren huddled on  board the sinking ship wearing  lifejackets but otherwise helpless just  waiting to be reached by rescuers many  lives were saved but many more are still  missing and the chances of finding any  more survivors including Kwon ji-yong as  parents are fading fast  Ashish Joshi sky news
 

